{"category_edits":[{"category":"training_strategy","rationale":"Replace validation-triggered learning-rate reductions with epoch-wise cosine decay, retaining Adam and the initial learning rate. If training reaches epoch 200, that epoch uses 10% of the initial rate. Preserve early stopping, batch size, dropout, weight decay, loss, architecture and per-category checkpoint selection.","edits":[{"find":"    scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(
        optimizer, mode="max", factor=0.5, patience=1,
        threshold=0.0, threshold_mode="abs", min_lr=LR * 0.125
    )","replace":"    scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(
        optimizer, T_max=max(NUM_EPOCHS - 1, 1), eta_min=LR * 0.1
    )"},{"find":"        avg_loss = total_loss / max(NUM_BATCHES, 1)","replace":"        if epoch < NUM_EPOCHS:
            scheduler.step()
        avg_loss = total_loss / max(NUM_BATCHES, 1)"},{"find":"            hr10 = val_m["HR@10"]
            scheduler.step(hr10)","replace":"            hr10 = val_m["HR@10"]"}]}],"change_summary":"Apply cosine learning-rate decay to each category’s single GRU model, with no inference changes."}
